230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 132 0 R
/T (Training, Validation, and Testing Strategy)
/E (Training, Validation, and Testing Strategy)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
231 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 505 0 R
/E (Ground Truth & Task Formulation: We use supervised link prediction on self-contained SC-MO-GRN-DB reference networks, treating each of the three evidence tiers as its own independent source without relying on external databases.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
232 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 506 0 R
/E (Strict Edge-Level Splitting: Positive edges are split strictly at the edge level, allocating 70% Train, 15% Validation, and 15% Test independently per tier via a fixed seed to guarantee zero leakage.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 507 0 R
/E (Disjoint Negative Sampling: Negative samples are random, non-regulatory TF-gene pairs drawn disjointly across splits, ensuring that a negative pair seen during training cannot reappear at test time.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 508 0 R
/E (Validation for Checkpointing: The 15% validation set is used actively during training to monitor AUPR, driving early stopping and selection of the best model checkpoint.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 509 0 R
/E (Held-Out Testing & Headline Metrics: The 15% test set is completely held out and evaluated only once for final reporting. We evaluate performance on all three tiers separately, but the high-confidence dual-evidence test set serves as our primary headline metric.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
